# CranePathOptimizer — Documentation Rules

The `docs/` folder is the project knowledge base. **Always consult it before coding.** Source code is truth; docs mirror implementation. Never treat planned features as implemented unless marked `[Planned Feature]`.

## Startup (every task)

1. Read `docs/agent/start-here.md` for routing.
2. **Mandatory:** `docs/agent/agent-context.md`, `docs/project/limitations.md`, `docs/ga/ga-settings-guide.md`.
3. Read task-specific docs from Section 3 of `start-here.md` (GA, IFC, DB, UI, architecture, refactoring).
4. **Verify in C#** — inspect implementing classes; do not assume docs are current without checking code.
5. Follow `docs/agent/definition-of-done.md` before considering work complete.

## Architecture (non-negotiable)

- **Clean Architecture:** Domain has zero outer dependencies. Application does not reference Infrastructure.
- **MVVM:** No business logic in `.xaml.cs`. ViewModels never reference WPF controls. Use `ViewModelBase`, `RelayCommand`, `AsyncRelayCommand`.
- **DI:** Register services in `App.xaml.cs`. Use repositories (`ICraneRepository`, `IProjectRepository`), not raw EF in Application/ViewModels.
- **DTO boundaries:** See `docs/coding-standards/dto-rules.md`.

## Never do (`docs/agent/do-not-do.md`)

- Block UI thread (`.Result`, `.Wait()`, `.GetAwaiter().GetResult()`).
- Run GA/IFC parsing on UI thread — use `Task.Run` / async.
- Reference outer layers from Domain; reference Views from ViewModels.
- Hardcode colors/fonts in XAML — use `Colors.xaml`, `Brushes.xaml`, `Typography.xaml` (Exo 2, terracotta `#D68A56`).
- Commit `.db` / `.sqlite` files.
- Instantiate `DbContext` in ViewModels.

